Z||000009||Matthew_Fiero||10-10-2001||08:32 AM||||Well, the stupid story is this<BR>I just turned 17, and i have only had my fiero for a couple of months. I decided to bleed the clutch. I look up on the forum to see what kind of transmittion fluid to put in the car, and i saw that it was 5w30, so i go to the store and feeling all happy cuz the bottle only cost 2 bucks. I get home and bleed it. The clutch feels better and i feel like it was a task well done. The next day, i open my master cylinder and the girling was twice the size, i found this odd, and try to reshape it back to what it looked like, and put it back in, later that day i open the cylinder again and not only wa it continuing to grow, it was in many many peices.  So  i just take it out thinking i wont need it. A couple days later i meet a new fiero friend and i tell him how my girling got warped for some reason. He happenes to have a spare one in a basket and gives it to me. Once again feeling joyful i pop in the new girling and i go back in the house.  The next day i decided to check on the girling and see that its doing the exact same thing! So i rip it out, head to the forum and ask why its doing this. Well i got my answer... i had put motor oil in instead of dot 3.  I felt like such an idiot  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> but i guess i learned my lesson... an expensive one, but i certainly will never do it again.<BR>So, can anyone top this stupid story?||||reg||1
Z||000010||Matthew_Fiero||10-10-2001||05:08 PM||||bump<BR>||||reg||1
