Z||000012||gt boy||10-10-2001||09:17 PM||||..no..I think you are the cream that has rose to the top.<P>...but i did put a 2-stoke motor together once and did not realize that i put the wrong crank seals in...plus put them in incorretly to boot....man did that sucker ever rev...<P><P>------------------<BR>"it's too bad he had to run out of talent half way through the corner..."||||reg||1
Z||000013||Fallman||10-11-2001||12:27 AM||||Hehehe well i cant top it but i sure as heck wish i would have bought a different fiero. i got my 86/87 GT for $1300. It needed a new engine so feeling all good thinking that i could do this in 2 days ripped the 2.8 out of a Chev celeb, that i had Killed the tranny on, Fortunatly it was the same model but when i went to change intake manifolds i found that the previous owner, of the celeb, had never changed the oil. Now this engine ran like a charm but IT HAD OIL BAKED ALLOVER THE INSIDE.  SO now im rebuilding that engine. finaly i get it rebuilt and in. GUESS WHAT??? The 3spd automatic slips in Second. So i pull it out and rebuild it only to put it back in and it still slips so i figure that its the pump. Anyway to make a longer story short im in search of a tranny. Now that i have more into the car then i think i can ever sell it for.<P>Brian<p>[This message has been edited by Fallman (edited 10-11-2001).]||||reg||1
